  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「カモガヤ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AB%E3%83%A2%E3%82%AC%E3%83%A4",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 108168278,
      "text": "カモガヤ はイネ科カモガヤ属の多年草。英名のオーチャードグラスでも流通する。和名のカモガヤ（鴨茅）は、英名の cock's-foot grass を訳すときに cock（ニワトリ）を duck（カモ）と間違えたといわれる。キヌイトソウ（絹糸草）ともいう。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Dactylis glomerata」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dactylis_glomerata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1367275754,
      "text": "Dactylis glomerata is a species of flowering plant in the grass family Poaceae, commonly known as barnyard grass, cocksfoot grass, cockspur, orchard grass, or cat grass (due to its popularity for use with domestic cats). It is a cool-season perennial C3 tufted grass native throughout most of Europe, temperate Asia, and northern Africa."
    }
  },
